    "title": "Walmart is selling an 'incredible' $248 43\" Roku Smart TV for just $178 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Liz Sheldon ,\n1 hours ago\nTheStreet aims to feature only the best products and services. If you buy something via one of our links, we may earn a commission.\nWhy we love this deal Not every day ends with hours to unwind after a long day, but when you do have time, sometimes it's great to be able to just relax and watch your favorite show. Plus, sometimes it's nice to use it as background noise while doing chores or streaming music while having guests over. Whatever you use your TV for, it's good to have one that you can count on.\nWith 4.4 stars from over 5,600 reviewers, you can count on the Onn 43-Inch 4K LED Roku Smart TV to have what you need, any time you need it. Plus, it's only $178 during Walmart's October deals event , which runs through Oct. 12.\nOnn 43-Inch 4K LED Roku Smart TV, $178 (was $248) at Walmart Courtesy of Walmart\nWhy do shoppers love it? This Onn TV features a 43-inch display with 4K resolution, which sharpens textures and brings the color to life. The LED panel is supported by HDR, giving the TV a large range of colors and contrast in both bright and dark pictures. The TV has a 60-hertz refresh rate that provides smooth motion and pictures while watching sports or gaming. It features three HDMI ports, one composite port, one USB port, one LAN port, one optical port, one headphone jack, and one coaxial port to plug the TV into your own cable box.\nRelated: Walmart is selling a $119 Bluetooth speaker for just $49, and customers love its sound quality for the size\nThe TV is integrated with the Roku Smart platform, offering over 500,000 shows and movies to stream across multiple platforms, so you can watch what you want when you want. It also offers a customizable home screen where you can add your favorite apps. All of this is available with the push of a button on the remote, or you can use your voice to easily search for your favorite shows. If that's not enough, in case you lost the remote, you can also use the free mobile app on your phone for voice control or browsing TV. It also works with Apple Home, Amazon Alexa, and Google Home. This TV also comes with a Roku remote, a quick start guide, and a stand with hardware to mount the TV. This TV size is great for the bedroom, family room, or game area. You can add your own apps, so you can also stream music, watch YouTube videos, and more.\nDetails to know Size: This is a 43-inch TV, measuring 42.5 actual inches diagonally. Controls: Use the included Roku remote buttons or voice control, or use the free Roku App on your phone to control the channels. Ports: It features three HDMI ports, one composite port, one USB port, one LAN port, one optical port, one headphone jack, and one coaxial port to plug the TV into your own cable box. One reviewer said, \"This TV is super easy to set up, literally just plug it in and sign in to your streaming subscriptions. The picture is amazing. Overall, incredible TV for a fantastic price.\" Another one said, \"We're very happy with this purchase. It has a very good picture and sound with an easy setup. You can add apps if you want extra programming.\"\nShop more deals TCL 43\" S4 4K UHD HDR Smart Roku TV, $198 (was $278) at Walmart Vizio 40\" Full HD 1080p LED Smart TV, $138 (was $170 at Walmart) Hisense 75\" Class 4K UHD LED Smart Roku TV, $478 (was $698) at Walmart The Onn 43-Inch 4K LED Roku Smart TV is a fantastic budget TV that offers tons of features for everyday use. Stream music for your next big party, watch the game with a clear, crisp picture and sound during football season, or just relax and easily find your favorite shows with the voice control.",
